    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0774" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14487.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Silliman</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-05T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1915—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Brazilian Minister, Mexico City, telegraphs International Relief Committee has
                    250,000 pesos for purchase supplies at Pachuca, San Juan del Rio and Apam, but
                    unable obtain railway transportation. Immediately request Carranza facilitate
                    transportation much needed supplies. Telegraph Minister result your efforts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
